Package: dr3
Title: Doubly-Robust ATE Estimators: Three Routes to One Answer
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R:
    person("M. Ehsan", "Karim", email = "ehsan.karim@ubc.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0346-2871"))
Description: A transparent, teaching-oriented reference implementation of the
    average treatment effect (ATE) estimators reconciled in "Three Routes to One
    Answer": g-computation, inverse-probability weighting, AIPW / one-step, and
    targeted maximum likelihood (TMLE), together with their cross-fit (double
    machine learning, CV-TMLE) and double-cross-fit (DC-AIPW, DC-TMLE) variants.
    Every estimator shares one Super Learner nuisance library, so differences
    between them come from the combination rule and the fitting scheme (and, for
    split-based estimators, from the random split), not from separate
    implementations. The package is meant for teaching and reproducibility and is cross-checked
    against the established 'tmle' and 'AIPW' packages, not as a replacement for
    them.
